Следующий код создаст бота Discord, использующий Discord.js v14 с одной слэш-командой для банирования пользователей:

1. Сначала установите зависимости:

```bash
npm install discord.js dotenv
```

2. Создайте `.env` файл и вставьте токен вашего бота в него:

```
TOKEN=<your bot token here>
```

3. Создайте новый файл `index.js` и вставьте следующий код:

```javascript
// Import required modules
const { Client, GatewayIntentBits, SlashCommandBuilder } = require('discord.js');
const { TOKEN } = require('./.env');

// Create a new Discord client instance
const client = new Client({
  intents: [
    GatewayIntentBits.Guilds,
    GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages,
    GatewayIntentBits.MessageContent,
  ],
});

// Define the ban command
const data = new SlashCommandBuilder()
  .setName('ban')
  .setDescription('Bans a user from the server.')
  .addUserOption((option) =>
    option
      .setName('user')
      .setDescription('The user to ban.')
      .setRequired(true)
  )
  .addStringOption((option) =>
    option
      .setName('reason')
      .setDescription('The reason for the ban.')
      .setRequired(false)
  );

// Register the command
client.on('ready', () => {
  client.application.commands.create({
    commandData: data,
    guild: client.guilds.cache.first(),
  });
});

// Handle the command
client.on('interactionCreate', async (interaction) => {
  if (!interaction.isCommand()) return;
  if (interaction.commandName === 'ban') {
    const user = interaction.options.getUser('user');
    const reason = interaction.options.getString('reason') || 'No reason provided';
    const member = interaction.guild.members.cache.get(user.id);

    if (!member) {
      return interaction.reply({
        content: `Could not find ${user} to ban.`,
        ephemeral: true,
      });
    }

    await member.ban({ reason });
    return interaction.reply({
      content: `${user} has been banned from this server for ${reason}.`,
    });
  }
});

// Login to Discord with your bot token
client.login(TOKEN);
```

4. Finally, run the bot using the following command:

```bash
node index.js
```

5. Make sure your bot has the `Ban Members` permission in the server where you want to use the ban command. You can manage bot permissions in the server settings under the "Members" tab.

That's it! Your Discord bot is now ready to use the ban command. Users can run it by typing `/ban @user [reason]` in a text channel. Replace `@user` with the user's Discord username and `reason` with an optional reason for the ban. The bot will respond with a message confirming the ban. If the user cannot be found, the bot will send an ephemeral message indicating the error.

Here's a possible implementation of a C++ function that takes a reference to a std::string containing text in a discounted format and returns a std::string containing the same text formatted in HTML:

```cpp
#include <string>

std::string discountToHtml(const std::string& discountText) {
    std::string htmlText;

    // Replace discount characters with their HTML equivalents
    for (char c : discountText) {
        switch (c) {
            case '_':
                htmlText += "<sub>";
                break;
            case '^':
                htmlText += "<sup>";
                break;
            case '$':
                htmlText += "<del>";
                break;
            case '%':
                htmlText += "<ins>";
                break;
            default:
                htmlText += c;
                break;
        }
        htmlText += c;
        if (c == '_' || c == '^') {
            htmlText += "</"+std::string(1, c)+">";
        }
    }

    return htmlText;
}
```

This function uses a simple switch statement to convert the discount characters (`_`, `^`, `$`, `%`) to their corresponding HTML tags (`<sub>`, `<sup>`, `<del>`, `<ins>`), respectively. It also adds the original character inside the tag to preserve the text.

Note that this implementation assumes that the input text contains only valid discount characters and that there are no nested tags. If you need more complex formatting, you may want to use a more robust library like Boost.Parsing or PugiXML.

